Олья.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:25.580
Now here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.040
Want to know a secret about passport?

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:29.460
Олья.

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:31.820
The Russian word, passport,

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:35.680
and the English word, passport are actually the same word.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:37.200
Олья.

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:39.160
They both come from Old French,

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:43.500
passport, which means pass through the port or gate.

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:44.940
Олья.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:48.020
This word started in medieval France,

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:50.840
traveled across Europe with kings and traders,

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:54.000
came into English and later arrived in Russian

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.780
during the time of Peter the Great.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:57.060
Олья.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.020
He wanted Russians to travel to Europe,

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.740
so the word came along, too.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:04.380
It kept almost the exact same spelling and meaning.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:05.740
Олья.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.240
This is a friendly cognate,

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:09.940
not a false friend.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:12.880
Many travel words in Russian are close to English,

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:15.460
like ballet, airport, and bagage.

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:16.920
Олья.

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:20.280
Next time you see the English word passport,

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:23.240
remember it is cousins with the Russian passport.

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:26.800
They both come from the old idea of passing the gate.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.740
That is your secret memory shortcut forever.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:32.200
Олья.

